gs":[],"url":"/docs/admin-spending#one-number-from-the-worksheet","content":"One number from the worksheet"},"6":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-4","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/admin-spending#why-a-newcomer-should-care","content":"Why a newcomer should care"},"7":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-5","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin-spending","content":"**Highlight 4 of 6** from the Sept 17 Commission worksheets."},"8":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-6","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin-spending#what-commissioners-were-asked","content":"The worksheet asked whether more Medicaid dollars are going to **administration, case management, contracts, and vendors** rather than **direct service** (the actual help a member receives)."},"9":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-7","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin-spending#important-caution","content":"HCPF materials did **not** identify this admin / middle layer as a driver of the spending growth being discussed. It was put on the table as a question — not as HCPF’s official explanation of the $1.26B growth."},"10":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-8","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin-spending#one-number-from-the-worksheet","content":"Case management spending was listed at **$161.2 million** in FY2025–26 across **96,259** members."},"11":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-9","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin-spending#one-number-from-the-worksheet","content":"Case management = coordinating plans and authorizations, not necessarily the person doing laundry or personal care. See Concepts to know first."},"12":{"id":"/docs/admin-spending-10","page_id":"/docs/admin-spending","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/admin-spending#why-a-newcomer-should-care","content":"This is an administrative sustainability opening: even